IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 5 Division 3, ss 175 and 175A -- the annual general meeting and when a private company need not hold one. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- It gives the keel's input for s 4(1) "annual general meeting" (`the meeting is a meeting of the company required to be held by section 175`).
-- The Minister's order under s 175(5) is machinery; its effect, a substituted number of months, is an input. The Registrar's extension under s 175(2)
-- is an official's decision; what it means to the company is the date to which the period is extended, also an input.
-- Taken as inputs from later waves: whether the company has sent the documents of s 203(1) in time (sgc1), whether the directors are exempt under s 201A (sgc1).

§ `Section 175(1): the duty to hold an annual general meeting`

-- "within (a) 4 months in the case of a public company that is listed; or (b) 6 months in the case of any other company". "Listed" is the keel's s 4(1) "listed".
-- The Minister's substitution (s 175(5)) is a number of months the person states (NOTHING if there is none).
-- src:15756 | 175.—(1) Subject to this section and section 175A, a company
-- src:15757 | must hold, in addition to any other meeting, a general meeting of the
-- src:15758 | company to be called the “annual general meeting” after the end of
-- src:15759 | each financial year within —
-- src:15761 | (a) 4 months in the case of a public company that is listed; or
-- src:15763 | (b) 6 months in the case of any other company.
@ref s 175(1) (src:15756-15763)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been removed from that official list` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of months the Minister has by order specified in substitution` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 175(1) and (5) the number of months within which the annual general meeting must be held` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the number of months the Minister has by order specified in substitution`
    WHEN JUST months THEN months
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
         IF `the company is a public company` AND (`s 4(1) "listed" the company or corporation is listed` `the company has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore` `the company has been removed from that official list` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         THEN 4
         ELSE 6

@ref s 175(1) (src:15756-15763)
GIVEN `the date the financial year ends` IS A DATE
      `the number of months within which the annual general meeting must be held` IS A NUMBER
      `the date to which the Registrar has extended the period` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 175(1) and (2) the last day for the annual general meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date to which the Registrar has extended the period`
    WHEN JUST extended THEN
         IF extended GREATER THAN (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the financial year ends` `the number of months within which the annual general meeting must be held` Months)
         THEN extended
         ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the financial year ends` `the number of months within which the annual general meeting must be held` Months
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the financial year ends` `the number of months within which the annual general meeting must be held` Months

@ref s 175(1) (src:15756-15763)
GIVEN `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year under section 175A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(1) the company must hold an annual general meeting for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year under section 175A`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to this section and section 175A, a company must hold ..." read with s 175A(1) "A company need not hold an annual general meeting for a financial year" (F-11)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- "after the end of each financial year within ..." : held after the year's end and not later than the last day. A period the text fixes: outside it, JUST FALSE (periods ruling (a)).
@ref s 175(1) (src:15756-15763)
GIVEN `the date the financial year ends` IS A DATE
      `the last day for the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the date the annual general meeting is held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(1) the annual general meeting is held in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the annual general meeting is held` GREATER THAN `the date the financial year ends` AND `the date the annual general meeting is held` AT MOST `the last day for the annual general meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a general meeting of the company to be called the 'annual general meeting' after the end of each financial year within (a) 4 months ...; or (b) 6 months" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling (a))

GIVEN `the date the financial year ends` IS A DATE
      `the last day for the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 175(1) the number of days from the end of the financial year to the last day for the annual general meeting` MEANS
    `the last day for the annual general meeting` MINUS `the date the financial year ends`

-- The keel's input for s 4(1) "annual general meeting": "a meeting of the company required to be held by section 175". A general meeting called the annual general meeting is that meeting where it
-- follows the end of a financial year (s 175(1)) or the company has resolved that it is the annual general meeting (s 175(3)).
@ref s 175(1) (src:15756-15763)
GIVEN `the meeting is a general meeting of the company called the annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is held after the end of a financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has resolved that the meeting is the annual general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(1) the meeting is the annual general meeting the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is a general meeting of the company called the annual general meeting` AND (`the meeting is held after the end of a financial year` OR `the company has resolved that the meeting is the annual general meeting of the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a general meeting of the company to be called the 'annual general meeting' after the end of each financial year" -- not a meeting of that description

§ `Section 175(2): the Registrar may extend the period`

-- What the Registrar's power means to the company: it may apply, and may ask for the extension of a prescribed class of companies to be applied. "upon an application by the company, if the Registrar thinks there are special reasons"
-- carries two gates, "upon" and "if"; the "if" governs, so a failure gives NOTHING (the grant ruling, limit 1; F-12, also listed under split site (ii)).
-- src:15767 | (2) The Registrar may extend the period mentioned in
-- src:15768 | subsection (1)(a) or (b) —
-- src:15773 | (a) upon an application by the company, if the Registrar thinks
-- src:15774 | there are special reasons to do so; or
-- src:15776 | (b) in respect of any prescribed class of companies.
@ref s 175(2) (src:15767-15776)
GIVEN `the company has applied to the Registrar for an extension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar thinks there are special reasons to extend the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is in a prescribed class of companies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(2) the Registrar may extend the period` MEANS
    IF (`the company has applied to the Registrar for an extension` AND `the Registrar thinks there are special reasons to extend the period`) OR `the company is in a prescribed class of companies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar may extend the period ... (a) upon an application by the company, if the Registrar thinks there are special reasons to do so; or (b) in respect of any prescribed class of companies" (a power whose gate failed; F-12)

§ `Section 175(3): any time, and the company may resolve that a meeting is the annual general meeting`

-- src:15780 | (3) Subject to notice being given to all persons entitled to receive
-- src:15781 | notice of the meeting, a general meeting may be held at any time and
-- src:15782 | the company may resolve that any meeting held or summoned to be
-- src:15783 | held is the annual general meeting of the company.
@ref s 175(3) (src:15780-15783)
GIVEN `notice has been given to all persons entitled to receive notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(3) a general meeting may be held at any time` MEANS
    IF `notice has been given to all persons entitled to receive notice of the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to notice being given to all persons entitled to receive notice of the meeting, a general meeting may be held at any time" (a grant whose gate failed; F-13)

@ref s 175(3) (src:15780-15783)
GIVEN `notice has been given to all persons entitled to receive notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting has been held or summoned to be held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(3) the company may resolve that the meeting is the annual general meeting` MEANS
    IF `notice has been given to all persons entitled to receive notice of the meeting` AND `the meeting has been held or summoned to be held`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to notice being given ..., the company may resolve that any meeting held or summoned to be held is the annual general meeting of the company" (F-13)

§ `Section 175(4): failure to hold the meeting`

-- src:15785 | (4) Where a company fails to comply with subsection (1) —
-- src:15787 | (a) the company and every officer of the company who is in
-- src:15788 | default shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:15789 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 and also to a
-- src:15790 | default penalty; and
-- src:15792 | (b) the Court may on the application of any member order a
-- src:15793 | general meeting to be called.
@ref s 175(4) (src:15785-15793)
GIVEN `the company has failed to comply with section 175(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(4)(a) the person is guilty of the offence this paragraph creates` MEANS
    IF `the company has failed to comply with section 175(1)` AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the paragraph's own question; split site (i), F-10): "Where a company fails to comply with subsection (1) (a) the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this paragraph makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts

@ref s 175(4)(a) (src:15785-15790)
GIVEN `the company has failed to comply with section 175(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 175(4)(a) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 175(4)(a) the person is guilty of the offence this paragraph creates` `the company has failed to comply with section 175(1)` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $5,000 and also a default penalty; no imprisonment
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (4)(b): "the Court may on the application of any member order a general meeting to be called". Gated by "Where a company fails to comply" and "on the application of any member":
-- a "where" gate on a "may", answered JUST FALSE as the periods ruling's rule (b) gives it (split site (ii); fork line F-14).
@ref s 175(4)(b) (src:15792-15793)
GIVEN `the company has failed to comply with section 175(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(4)(b) the Court may on the application of the member order a general meeting to be called` MEANS
    IF `the company has failed to comply with section 175(1)` AND `the applicant is a member of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company fails to comply with subsection (1) ... the Court may on the application of any member order a general meeting to be called" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b), "where"; split site (ii), F-14)

§ `Section 175A(1): a company that need not hold an annual general meeting`

-- src:15805 | 175A.—(1) A company need not hold an annual general meeting
-- src:15806 | for a financial year —
-- src:15808 | (a) if it is a private company in respect of which there is in
-- src:15809 | force a resolution passed in accordance with subsection (2)
-- src:15810 | to dispense with the holding of annual general meetings;
@ref s 175A(1)(a) (src:15805-15810)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a resolution passed in accordance with section 175A(2) to dispense with the holding of annual general meetings is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175A(1)(a) the company need not hold an annual general meeting because of a resolution in force` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private company` AND `a resolution passed in accordance with section 175A(2) to dispense with the holding of annual general meetings is in force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) if it is a private company in respect of which there is in force a resolution passed in accordance with subsection (2) to dispense with the holding of annual general meetings" (an "if" gate failed; marginal reading (a), F-15)

-- src:15812 | (b) if, at the end of that financial year, it is a private company
-- src:15813 | and has sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of
-- src:15814 | general meetings of the company the documents
-- src:15815 | mentioned in section 203(1) within the period specified
-- src:15816 | in section 203(1)(b); or
@ref s 175A(1)(b) (src:15812-15816)
GIVEN `at the end of the financial year the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company the documents mentioned in section 203(1) within the period specified in section 203(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175A(1)(b) the company need not hold an annual general meeting because it has sent the documents` MEANS
    IF `at the end of the financial year the company is a private company` AND `the company has sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company the documents mentioned in section 203(1) within the period specified in section 203(1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if, at the end of that financial year, it is a private company and has sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company the documents mentioned in section 203(1) within the period specified in section 203(1)(b)" (an "if" gate failed; F-15)

-- src:15818 | (c) if, at the end of that financial year, it is both a private
-- src:15819 | company and a dormant relevant company the directors of
-- src:15824 | which are, under section 201A, exempt from the
-- src:15825 | requirements of section 201 for the financial year.
@ref s 175A(1)(c) (src:15818-15825)
GIVEN `at the end of the financial year the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the end of the financial year the company is a dormant relevant company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors of the company are, under section 201A, exempt from the requirements of section 201 for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175A(1)(c) the company need not hold an annual general meeting because it is a dormant relevant company` MEANS
    IF `at the end of the financial year the company is a private company` AND `at the end of the financial year the company is a dormant relevant company` AND `the directors of the company are, under section 201A, exempt from the requirements of section 201 for the financial year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) if, at the end of that financial year, it is both a private company and a dormant relevant company the directors of which are, under section 201A, exempt from the requirements of section 201 for the financial year" (an "if" gate failed; F-15)

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      c IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175A(1) the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year` MEANS
    IF a EQUALS JUST TRUE OR b EQUALS JUST TRUE OR c EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company need not hold an annual general meeting for a financial year (a) if ...; (b) if ...; or (c) if ..." -- none of the three "if" gates holds (F-15)

§ `Section 175A(2) and (3): the resolution to dispense with annual general meetings`

-- (2): "a resolution mentioned in subsection (1)(a) is only treated as passed at a general meeting if it has been passed by all of such members as, being entitled to do so, vote in person or, where proxies
-- are allowed, by proxy present at the meeting". "only ... if": a closed gate, JUST FALSE. If nobody voted, "all of such members" is vacuous; a resolution nobody voted for is not passed (F-16).
-- src:15829 | (2) Despite any other provision of this Act, a resolution mentioned
-- src:15830 | in subsection (1)(a) is only treated as passed at a general meeting if it
-- src:15831 | has been passed by all of such members as, being entitled to do so,
-- src:15832 | vote in person or, where proxies are allowed, by proxy present at the
-- src:15833 | meeting.
@ref s 175A(2) (src:15829-15833)
GIVEN `the number of members who, being entitled to do so, vote in person or by proxy present at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those members who vote for the resolution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175A(2) the resolution is treated as passed at a general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the number of members who, being entitled to do so, vote in person or by proxy present at the meeting` AT LEAST 1
       AND `the number of those members who vote for the resolution` EQUALS `the number of members who, being entitled to do so, vote in person or by proxy present at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a resolution mentioned in subsection (1)(a) is only treated as passed at a general meeting if it has been passed by all of such members as, being entitled to do so, vote in person or, where proxies are allowed, by proxy present at the meeting" ("only if"; F-16)

-- src:15837 | (3) A resolution under subsection (1)(a) has effect for the year in
-- src:15838 | which it is made and subsequent years, but does not affect any
-- src:15839 | liability already incurred by reason of default in holding an annual
-- src:15840 | general meeting.
@ref s 175A(3) (src:15837-15840)
GIVEN `the financial year in which the resolution was made` IS A NUMBER
      `the financial year asked about` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175A(3) the resolution has effect for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `the financial year asked about` AT LEAST `the financial year in which the resolution was made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "has effect for the year in which it is made and subsequent years" says nothing of an earlier year

@ref s 175A(3) (src:15837-15840)
GIVEN `the liability was incurred before the resolution by reason of default in holding an annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175A(3) the resolution affects the liability` MEANS
    IF `the liability was incurred before the resolution by reason of default in holding an annual general meeting`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect any liability already incurred by reason of default in holding an annual general meeting" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text speaks only of a liability already incurred by reason of default in holding an annual general meeting

§ `Section 175A(4) to (6): a member may require an annual general meeting`

-- src:15844 | (4) In any year in which an annual general meeting would be
-- src:15845 | required to be held but for this section, and in which no such meeting
-- src:15846 | has been held, any member of the company may, by notice to the
-- src:15847 | company not later than 14 days before the date by which an annual
-- src:15848 | general meeting would have been required under section 175 to be
-- src:15849 | held, require the holding of an annual general meeting in that year.
@ref s 175A(4) (src:15844-15849)
GIVEN `the date by which an annual general meeting would have been required under section 175 to be held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 175A(4) the latest day for the member's notice` MEANS
    `period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the date by which an annual general meeting would have been required under section 175 to be held` 14 Days

-- A power of the member whose scope is "any member", "in any year in which an annual general meeting would be required but for this section, and in which no such meeting has been held": a person or year
-- outside the scope gets NOTHING (periods ruling (c)); within it, the 14-day limit is a period the text fixes, so a late notice gets JUST FALSE (periods ruling (a)).
@ref s 175A(4) (src:15844-15849)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an annual general meeting would be required to be held in the year but for section 175A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no annual general meeting has been held in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date by which an annual general meeting would have been required under section 175 to be held` IS A DATE
      `the date the member gave notice to the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175A(4) the member may by notice require the holding of an annual general meeting` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is a member of the company` AND `an annual general meeting would be required to be held in the year but for section 175A` AND `no annual general meeting has been held in the year`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any year in which an annual general meeting would be required to be held but for this section, and in which no such meeting has been held, any member of the company may" (a scope limit with no "only"; periods ruling (c); F-17)
    ELSE (IF `the date the member gave notice to the company` AT MOST (`s 175A(4) the latest day for the member's notice` `the date by which an annual general meeting would have been required under section 175 to be held`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by notice to the company not later than 14 days before the date by which an annual general meeting would have been required under section 175 to be held" (a period the text fixes; periods ruling (a))

-- src:15853 | (5) The power of a member under subsection (4) to require the
-- src:15854 | holding of an annual general meeting is exercisable not only by the
-- src:15855 | giving of a notice but also by the transmission to the company at such
-- src:15856 | address as may for the time being be specified for the purpose by or
-- src:15857 | on behalf of the company of an electronic communication containing
-- src:15858 | the requirement.
@ref s 175A(5) (src:15853-15858)
GIVEN `the member gave notice to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member transmitted to the company an electronic communication containing the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the electronic communication was transmitted to the address specified for the purpose by or on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175A(5) the member has exercised the power under subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `the member gave notice to the company` OR (`the member transmitted to the company an electronic communication containing the requirement` AND `the electronic communication was transmitted to the address specified for the purpose by or on behalf of the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "exercisable not only by the giving of a notice but also by the transmission to the company at such address as may for the time being be specified ... of an electronic communication containing the requirement" names two ways without saying "only"

-- src:15860 | (6) If such a notice is given or electronic communication is
-- src:15861 | transmitted, section 175(1) and (4) applies with respect to the calling
-- src:15862 | of the meeting and the consequences of any failure to comply with
-- src:15863 | section 175(1) as applied by this subsection.
@ref s 175A(6) (src:15860-15863)
GIVEN `a notice has been given under subsection (4) or an electronic communication has been transmitted under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175A(6) section 175(1) and (4) apply to the calling of the meeting and the consequences of failure` MEANS
    IF `a notice has been given under subsection (4) or an electronic communication has been transmitted under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If such a notice is given or electronic communication is transmitted, section 175(1) and (4) applies" (an "if" gate failed; marginal reading (a), F-15)

§ `Section 175A(7) to (9): when the resolution ceases`

-- src:15867 | (7) A resolution mentioned in subsection (1)(a) ceases to be in force
-- src:15868 | if the company is converted to a public company.
@ref s 175A(7) (src:15867-15868)
GIVEN `the company is converted to a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175A(7) the resolution has ceased to be in force` MEANS
    IF `the company is converted to a public company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ceases to be in force if the company is converted to a public company" (an "if" gate failed; marginal reading (a), F-15: the subsection does not say the resolution can cease only on conversion)

-- (8): "If the resolution ... ceases to be in force but less than 3 months remain to the date on which the company is required under section 175 to hold an annual general meeting, the company need not hold that annual general meeting."
-- Less than 3 months remain when the day it ceased is later than the latest day that is 3 months before the deadline (P5), and not after the deadline.
-- src:15872 | (8) If the resolution mentioned in subsection (1)(a) ceases to be in
-- src:15873 | force but less than 3 months remain to the date on which the company
-- src:15878 | is required under section 175 to hold an annual general meeting, the
-- src:15879 | company need not hold that annual general meeting.
@ref s 175A(8) (src:15872-15879)
GIVEN `the date the resolution ceased to be in force` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company is required under section 175 to hold an annual general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175A(8) the company need not hold the annual general meeting after the resolution ceased` MEANS
    IF    `the date the resolution ceased to be in force` GREATER THAN (`period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the date on which the company is required under section 175 to hold an annual general meeting` 3 Months)
      AND `the date the resolution ceased to be in force` AT MOST `the date on which the company is required under section 175 to hold an annual general meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the resolution ... ceases to be in force but less than 3 months remain to the date on which the company is required under section 175 to hold an annual general meeting, the company need not hold that annual general meeting" (an "if" gate failed)

-- src:15883 | (9) Subsection (8) does not affect any obligation of the company to
-- src:15884 | hold an annual general meeting in that year pursuant to a notice given
-- src:15885 | under subsection (4) or an electronic communication transmitted
-- src:15886 | under subsection (5).
@ref s 175A(9) (src:15883-15886)
GIVEN `the member gave notice under subsection (4) or transmitted an electronic communication under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175A(9) subsection (8) relieves the company of the meeting the member required` MEANS
    IF `the member gave notice under subsection (4) or transmitted an electronic communication under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (8) does not affect any obligation of the company to hold an annual general meeting in that year pursuant to a notice given under subsection (4) or an electronic communication transmitted under subsection (5)" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (9) speaks only of an obligation arising from such a notice or communication

§ `Section 175A(10) and (11): how references are read, and the word address`

DECLARE `s 175A(10) reference` IS ONE OF
    `s 175A(10)(a) a reference to the doing of anything at an annual general meeting`
    `s 175A(10)(b) a reference to the date or conclusion of an annual general meeting`
    `s 175A(10)(c) the reference in section 197(1) or (1A) to the lodging of a return with the Registrar after its annual general meeting`

DECLARE `s 175A(10) reading` IS ONE OF
    `s 175A(10)(a) read as the doing of that thing by way of a resolution by written means under section 184A`
    `s 175A(10)(b) read as the date of expiry of the period by which an annual general meeting would have been required under section 175 to be held`
    `s 175A(10)(c)(i) read as the lodging of the return after the company has sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings the documents mentioned in section 203(1)`
    `s 175A(10)(c)(ii) read as the lodging of the return after the end of its financial year`
    `s 175A(10) the reference is not read differently`

-- The "reading" is what the reference is to be read as. "not read differently" is the text's no: "Unless the contrary intention appears", "if a company need not hold", and for (b) "unless the meeting is held".
-- src:15888 | (10) Unless the contrary intention appears, if a company need not
-- src:15889 | hold an annual general meeting for a financial year then for that
-- src:15890 | financial year —
-- src:15892 | (a) a reference in any provision of this Act to the doing of
-- src:15893 | anything at an annual general meeting is to be read as a
-- src:15894 | reference to the doing of that thing by way of a resolution
-- src:15895 | by written means under section 184A;
-- src:15897 | (b) a reference in any provision of this Act to the date or
-- src:15898 | conclusion of an annual general meeting is, unless the
-- src:15899 | meeting is held, to be read as a reference to the date of
-- src:15900 | expiry of the period by which an annual general meeting
-- src:15901 | would have been required under section 175 to be held;
-- src:15903 | (c) the reference in section 197(1) or (1A) to the lodging of a
-- src:15904 | return with the Registrar after its annual general meeting is
-- src:15905 | to be read as a reference to the lodging of that return —
-- src:15907 | (i) in the case of a company mentioned in
-- src:15908 | subsection (1)(a) or (b) — after the company has
-- src:15909 | sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of
-- src:15910 | general meetings of the company the documents
-- src:15911 | mentioned in section 203(1); or
-- src:15913 | (ii) in the case of a company mentioned in
-- src:15914 | subsection (1)(c) — after the end of its financial year.
@ref s 175A(10) (src:15888-15914)
GIVEN reference IS A `s 175A(10) reference`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the annual general meeting is held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is mentioned in section 175A(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is mentioned in section 175A(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 175A(10) reading`
`s 175A(10) how the reference is read for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `a contrary intention appears` OR (NOT `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year`)
    THEN JUST `s 175A(10) the reference is not read differently`   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the contrary intention appears, if a company need not hold an annual general meeting for a financial year then for that financial year"
    ELSE CONSIDER reference
         WHEN `s 175A(10)(a) a reference to the doing of anything at an annual general meeting` THEN JUST `s 175A(10)(a) read as the doing of that thing by way of a resolution by written means under section 184A`
         WHEN `s 175A(10)(b) a reference to the date or conclusion of an annual general meeting` THEN
              IF `the annual general meeting is held`
              THEN JUST `s 175A(10) the reference is not read differently`   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, unless the meeting is held, to be read as a reference to the date of expiry of the period ..."
              ELSE JUST `s 175A(10)(b) read as the date of expiry of the period by which an annual general meeting would have been required under section 175 to be held`
         WHEN `s 175A(10)(c) the reference in section 197(1) or (1A) to the lodging of a return with the Registrar after its annual general meeting` THEN
              IF `the company is mentioned in section 175A(1)(a) or (b)`
              THEN JUST `s 175A(10)(c)(i) read as the lodging of the return after the company has sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings the documents mentioned in section 203(1)`
              ELSE (IF `the company is mentioned in section 175A(1)(c)`
                    THEN JUST `s 175A(10)(c)(ii) read as the lodging of the return after the end of its financial year`
                    ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (c) reads the reference for a company mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) and says nothing of any other

-- src:15918 | (11) In this section, an address of a person includes any number or
-- src:15919 | address used for electronic communication.
@ref s 175A(11) (src:15918-15919)
GIVEN `the thing is a number or address used for electronic communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175A(11) the thing is within the word address of a person` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a number or address used for electronic communication`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "an address of a person includes any number or address used for electronic communication"

§ `Regulative rule: the duty of s 175(1)`

DECLARE `s 175 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 175(1) hold the annual general meeting`

-- The clock: time 0 is the day the financial year ends; the last day is given in days from it (s 175(1) number of days).
-- src:15756 | 175.—(1) Subject to this section and section 175A, a company
-- src:15757 | must hold, in addition to any other meeting, a general meeting of the
-- src:15758 | company to be called the “annual general meeting” after the end of
-- src:15759 | each financial year within —
-- src:15761 | (a) 4 months in the case of a public company that is listed; or
-- src:15763 | (b) 6 months in the case of any other company.
@ref s 175(1) (src:15756-15763)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from the end of the financial year to the last day for the annual general meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 175 act`
`s 175(1) the company must hold the annual general meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 175(1) hold the annual general meeting`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the end of the financial year to the last day for the annual general meeting`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not hold the annual general meeting within the period section 175(1) allows after the end of the financial year"
